{
  "_design": [
    "Every medium that prints a canonical figure, and how it is checked.",
    "",
    "kind=repo     : a file CI can read. CHECK C asserts the current",
    "                print_precision of each declared key appears in it.",
    "kind=external : CI cannot reach it. It carries a human attestation that",
    "                EXPIRES: any attestation older than canonical.json's",
    "                generated_at fails CHECK C. Stamp one with",
    "                  scripts/gate_canon.sh attest \"<medium>\" \"<name>\"",
    "                after actually comparing the medium against canonical.json.",
    "kind=absent   : named in the cascade but not present here. Reported as a",
    "                notice so its absence is visible rather than inferred.",
    "",
    "A medium's `keys` list is a claim about what it carries. Adding a figure to",
    "a medium without adding the key here leaves that figure unpoliced, so the",
    "list is the thing to update when a medium starts printing a new number."
